  "observations": [
    "The six initial association, refresh, failure, loading, retry and second-page images are actually dark despite their historical light filename suffix. They are counted as dark visual evidence only.",
    "Associations show the fixed and archived conversations. Refresh shows the renamed conversation. Full repository read errors and the disabled refresh/loading message are visible while remaining repositories retain their rows.",
    "The retry image shows only the top settings fields and does not visually establish the refreshed list. The second-page image shows the project heading and 23-tree count, but not the lower page controls.",
    "All six explicit light/dark 100/125/150-percent errors show the complete red error. All six corresponding row images show complete blue outlines around the expanded conversation summary.",
    "At 125 percent lower row actions require scrolling. At 150 percent paths wrap and lower sidebar categories, rows and pagination require independent vertical scrolling.",
    "The automatic-cleanup-off count explanation is visible in the loading, second-page and 100-percent views. None of these 18 images captures the no-project empty heading/body."
  ],
  "scope": "Current packaged overview visual scope only. The original complete 355-check run separately establishes refresh, pagination, isolation and preservation. No-project empty-state images, independent repository/conversation loading reference differences and complete reference adoption remain unverified."
